Package: MultipleSystemsEstimation
Title: Multiple Systems Estimation with Sparse Capture Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
  given = c("Bernard", "W."),
  family = "Silverman",
  email = "bernard.silverman@stats.ox.ac.uk",
  role = c("aut", "cre") ),
    person("Lax", "Chan",
           role = "ctb"),
    person("Kyle", "Vincent",
           role = "ctb")
    )
Description: Methods for multiple systems estimation using Poisson log-linear
    models, with particular attention to sparse capture data, and to ensuring that
    the estimation uncertainty includes the uncertainty
    arising from model selection. The package implements methodology from
    Chan, Silverman and Vincent (2021) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2019.1708748> and
    Silverman, Chan and Vincent (2024)
    <doi:10.1007/s11222-023-10346-9>.
URL: https://bernardsilverman.github.io/MultipleSystemsEstimation/,
        https://bernardsilverman.co.uk/contact,
        https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.2019.1708748,
        https://doi.org/10.1007/s11222-023-10346-9
